WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.000
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:02:17.716 --> 00:02:21.820
It's two plus two
equals six.


00:02:24.354 --> 00:02:26.691
I will never tell you.


00:02:26.721 --> 00:02:27.893
But you will.


00:02:28.031 --> 00:02:33.228
OPERATION DUNKIRK


00:02:34.191 --> 00:02:37.691
Subrip: Pix
<font color=#ff0000>subs4free.info</font>


00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:11.173
<i>The enemy attacked us
on all sides</i>


00:03:11.203 --> 00:03:13.775
<i>with great strength
and fierceness.</i>


00:03:13.805 --> 00:03:16.745
<i>Pressing in upon
the narrow exit,</i>


00:03:16.775 --> 00:03:18.947
<i>both from the east
and from the west,</i>


00:03:18.977 --> 00:03:22.183
<i>the enemy began
to fire with cannon</i>


00:03:22.213 --> 00:03:24.816
<i>upon the beaches by
which alone the shipping</i>


00:03:24.846 --> 00:03:27.588
<i>could approach or depart.</i>


00:03:27.618 --> 00:03:30.672
<i>Meanwhile, the Royal Navy
with the willing help</i>


00:03:30.702 --> 00:03:33.757
<i>of countless Merchant
Seamen strained</i>


00:03:33.758 --> 00:03:38.796
<i>every nerve to embark
the British and Allied troops.</i>


00:03:38.826 --> 00:03:42.037
<i>Two-hundred and twenty light
warships</i>


00:03:42.067 --> 00:03:46.275
<i>and 650 other vessels
were engaged.</i>


00:03:46.305 --> 00:03:48.840
<i>They had to operate
upon a difficult coast</i>


00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:52.246
<i>often in adverse weather</i>


00:03:52.276 --> 00:03:56.214
<i>under an almost
ceaseless hail of bombs</i>


00:03:56.215 --> 00:04:00.485
<i>and an increasing concentration
of artillery fire.</i>


00:04:00.515 --> 00:04:02.824
<i>Nor were the seas,
as I have said,</i>


00:04:02.854 --> 00:04:05.926
<i>themselves free
from mines and torpedoes.</i>


00:04:05.956 --> 00:04:08.492
<i>It was in conditions
such as these that our men</i>


00:04:08.522 --> 00:04:11.912
<i>carried on with
little or no rest.</i>


00:04:11.942 --> 00:04:15.303
<i>For days and nights on end,</i>


00:04:15.333 --> 00:04:19.340
<i>making trip after trip
across the dangerous waters,</i>


00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:23.608
<i>bringing with them always
men whom they had rescued.</i>


00:04:46.497 --> 00:04:48.550
Attention!


00:04:48.580 --> 00:04:50.604
At ease.


00:04:50.634 --> 00:04:53.474
Lt. Calloway?


00:04:53.504 --> 00:04:56.192
This must be your lucky day.


00:04:56.222 --> 00:04:58.881
You're not being evacuated.


00:04:58.911 --> 00:05:01.831
You might actually
live another day.


00:05:01.861 --> 00:05:04.675
It's a ruddy
bloodbath out there!


00:05:04.705 --> 00:05:07.489
Gentlemen, battles
will be won


00:05:07.519 --> 00:05:10.120
by the side that
first spots enemy airplanes,


00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:12.159
ships or submarines.


00:05:12.189 --> 00:05:14.526
And British scientists have
been working feverishly


00:05:14.556 --> 00:05:17.561
to develop radar
technology that will see


00:05:17.591 --> 00:05:20.597
for hundreds of miles,
even at night.


00:05:20.598 --> 00:05:24.304
But they haven't been
able to crack it.


00:05:24.334 --> 00:05:26.837
Just recently, we got
intelligence from the Americans.


00:05:26.838 --> 00:05:28.306
The Americans?


00:05:28.336 --> 00:05:29.643
Yes.


00:05:29.673 --> 00:05:32.476
Seems a German scientist
has developed this technology


00:05:32.506 --> 00:05:35.279
but doesn't want
to share it with Hitler.


00:05:35.309 --> 00:05:37.184
I know.


00:05:37.214 --> 00:05:39.253
Whatever his reasons,
he wants to share it with us.


00:05:39.283 --> 00:05:43.788
Therefore, I need you and your
men to go retrieve the package.


00:05:43.818 --> 00:05:45.856
The package being?


00:05:45.857 --> 00:05:47.794
The German scientist.


00:05:47.824 --> 00:05:49.729
Do we know where this
package is, sir?


00:05:49.759 --> 00:05:51.898
Yes. We're being told
the French Resistance has


00:05:51.928 --> 00:05:55.332
the German scientist in a
safe house not far from here.


00:05:55.333 --> 00:06:00.706
He's being held here
in an old factory


00:06:00.736 --> 00:06:03.410
right off of L'Autoroute A25.


00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:06.179
That's 51 degrees north,
37 east.


00:06:06.209 --> 00:06:09.079
You're to go there,
rendezvous with the French,


00:06:09.109 --> 00:06:11.915
retrieve the package,
and get out.


00:06:11.945 --> 00:06:13.354
Any questions?


00:06:13.384 --> 00:06:15.687
Much enemy activity
in the area, sir?


00:06:15.717 --> 00:06:18.039
From our reports,
little to none.


00:06:18.069 --> 00:06:20.391
The French are
expecting you.


00:06:20.421 --> 00:06:22.296
Once you've made contact,


00:06:22.326 --> 00:06:24.528
they will ask you for
a piece of paper.


00:06:24.558 --> 00:06:26.730
Give them this.


00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:28.236
Sir.


00:06:28.266 --> 00:06:29.970
Any more questions?


00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.204
So we're not going to be
evacuated, then. Is that it?


00:06:33.234 --> 00:06:35.873
You have your orders.


00:06:35.874 --> 00:06:39.210
Pull your balls out of your
throat and be a soldier!


00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:41.111
- Yes, sir!
- Get your kit together


00:06:41.112 --> 00:06:43.382
and get ready to move out.
Do you understand me?


00:06:43.412 --> 00:06:44.483
Yes, sir!


00:06:46.384 --> 00:06:50.588
This mission could
not only save lives,


00:06:50.618 --> 00:06:52.057
but win the war.


00:06:53.925 --> 00:06:56.028
Carry on.


00:07:07.137 --> 00:07:09.106
You heard the colonel.


00:07:09.107 --> 00:07:11.242
Little to no enemy activity.


00:07:11.272 --> 00:07:12.313
We get in, we get out.


00:07:12.343 --> 00:07:14.482
We don't miss the evacuation.


00:07:14.512 --> 00:07:17.281
Just one last roll
of the dice, lads.


00:07:22.519 --> 00:07:23.621
Let's go.


00:08:19.943 --> 00:08:22.764
Should be just over
this field.


00:08:22.794 --> 00:08:25.616
Better proceed
with caution.


00:09:10.294 --> 00:09:12.197
Into the bushes!


00:09:50.467 --> 00:09:53.471
You must love your
family very much, no?


00:09:55.472 --> 00:09:57.475
Do you realize that
we know where they are?


00:09:59.277 --> 00:10:03.948
My soldiers are on their way
right now to pick them up.


00:10:03.978 --> 00:10:07.852
<i>Mein familia has
nothing to do with this!</i>


00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:23.634
No!


00:10:30.251 --> 00:10:33.588
Tell me!


00:10:51.714 --> 00:10:55.087
Okay.
Okay.


00:10:55.117 --> 00:10:58.289
I give it
to a young woman,


00:10:58.319 --> 00:11:03.825
French Resistance
on her way to BAF now.


00:11:12.166 --> 00:11:14.436
Angelique!


00:11:19.940 --> 00:11:22.243
Show me where she is.


00:11:41.530 --> 00:11:45.800
They will see you
soon enough.


00:12:21.596 --> 00:12:23.433
Everything all right, Thomas?


00:12:23.463 --> 00:12:26.200
It's my son's birthday
in two weeks.


00:12:26.201 --> 00:12:29.573
I just really
wanted to see him.


00:12:29.603 --> 00:12:33.541
I haven't seen him
yet since he was born.


00:12:36.276 --> 00:12:37.711
Don't worry about it,
Thomas.


00:12:37.712 --> 00:12:40.867
You'll see him on his
next birthday, yeah?


00:12:40.897 --> 00:12:43.510
You can tell him what
a hero his father is.


00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:46.154
Never actually been
with a woman myself.


00:12:46.184 --> 00:12:48.088
You never been with a woman?


00:12:48.118 --> 00:12:50.157
Not intimately, no.


00:12:50.158 --> 00:12:52.828
So you've not had a shag?


00:12:52.858 --> 00:12:55.529
Such a romantic, Walker.


00:13:00.034 --> 00:13:01.273
Let's just find this kraut,


00:13:01.303 --> 00:13:03.505
and get the hell
out of France, yeah?


00:13:03.535 --> 00:13:05.275
What do you say?


00:13:05.305 --> 00:13:08.210
I hate this country.
It stinks.


00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:11.115
Lieutenant, all due respect,


00:13:11.145 --> 00:13:13.914
how do we know we can
trust this scientist?


00:13:13.944 --> 00:13:16.687
He is German, after all.


00:13:16.717 --> 00:13:20.053
Because cleverer men
than us have told us so.


00:13:20.083 --> 00:13:22.122
Well, they better be right.


00:13:24.058 --> 00:13:25.994
This must be it, lads.


00:13:29.329 --> 00:13:30.431
Stay sharp.


00:13:54.789 --> 00:13:56.609
Drop your weapons!


00:13:56.639 --> 00:14:00.894
Lower your guns!


00:14:00.895 --> 00:14:02.831
I said drop your guns!


00:14:02.861 --> 00:14:04.798
Turn!


00:14:04.799 --> 00:14:06.134
Turn slowly to me!


00:14:10.704 --> 00:14:11.742
Turn slowly!


00:14:11.772 --> 00:14:13.474
What is your business here?


00:14:15.343 --> 00:14:18.213
We're with the British
Expeditionary Force.


00:14:18.243 --> 00:14:20.531
We've come
to collect a package.


00:14:20.561 --> 00:14:22.850
You should have
a package for me.


00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:25.352
Yes. Yes, I do.


00:14:40.568 --> 00:14:41.606
Read it.


00:14:41.636 --> 00:14:43.805
Read it to me!


00:14:48.309 --> 00:14:50.729
"The children long
to play in the fields


00:14:50.759 --> 00:14:53.150
but had to settle
instead for the sand


00:14:53.180 --> 00:14:56.350
which was accompanied
by an enormous roar."


00:14:56.380 --> 00:14:59.586
All right, where is he?


00:14:59.587 --> 00:15:01.924
How many are with you?


00:15:01.954 --> 00:15:04.292
Just the five of us.


00:15:07.027 --> 00:15:08.829
All right, where is he?


00:15:08.859 --> 00:15:11.499
She is inside.


00:15:13.834 --> 00:15:16.469
Wait. She?


00:15:17.705 --> 00:15:19.173
You did not know.


00:15:19.174 --> 00:15:21.275
No. I thought we were
collecting the chap


00:15:21.305 --> 00:15:24.127
with the algorithm
for radar.


00:15:24.157 --> 00:15:26.938
You were until
he was captured


00:15:26.968 --> 00:15:29.749
by Nazi but moments
before this.


00:15:29.779 --> 00:15:30.951
He gave the algorithm.


00:15:30.981 --> 00:15:32.285
To Angelique.


00:15:32.286 --> 00:15:33.954
Angelique?


00:15:35.256 --> 00:15:38.927
<i>- Oui.
- All right, let's go.</i>


00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:07.991
Angelique?


00:16:08.021 --> 00:16:09.160
<i>C'est moi, Pierre.</i>


00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:12.727
Don't shoot, don't shoot.


00:16:12.757 --> 00:16:15.500
This is her.


00:16:15.530 --> 00:16:16.700
You have the algorithm?


00:16:16.730 --> 00:16:19.833
<i>- Oui.
- May I see it?</i>


00:16:19.834 --> 00:16:23.404
I have not written it down.
So you must keep me alive.


00:16:23.434 --> 00:16:25.038
Very sensible.


00:16:25.039 --> 00:16:26.741
Then we should leave.


00:16:26.771 --> 00:16:27.979
What's the plan?


00:16:28.009 --> 00:16:30.612
We must get her
to this location.


00:16:30.642 --> 00:16:32.346
They will further assist her.


00:16:32.347 --> 00:16:36.050
They have arranged a plane
to take her to Great Britain.


00:16:36.080 --> 00:16:40.788
But we must wait
for the Americans.


00:16:40.818 --> 00:16:42.726
They're already late.


00:16:42.756 --> 00:16:44.358
So I'm assuming the worst.


00:16:44.388 --> 00:16:45.560
We need to move.


00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:49.330
Shit! We've got company!


00:16:52.032 --> 00:16:54.636
So much for little
to no enemy activity.


00:16:54.666 --> 00:16:55.807
Take cover.


00:16:55.837 --> 00:16:57.623
I'll see if I
can delay them.


00:16:57.653 --> 00:16:59.409
All right,
let's dig in, lads.


00:16:59.439 --> 00:17:02.108
We were given a mission
and I plan on completing it.


00:17:02.138 --> 00:17:04.044
Harris, get me the colonel
on the wireless.


00:17:04.074 --> 00:17:05.282
Yes, sir.


00:17:05.312 --> 00:17:09.251
F13C here.
Come in, Dunkirk.


00:17:09.281 --> 00:17:13.221
F13C.
This is Colonel Plummer.


00:17:13.251 --> 00:17:15.056
Sir, I have the colonel.


00:17:18.393 --> 00:17:20.995
We're at the destination, sir.
But the package isn't here.


00:17:21.025 --> 00:17:22.433
<i>There is a French girl
with the Resistance.</i>


00:17:22.463 --> 00:17:24.531
<i>Said she was given
the algorithm by the scientist</i>


00:17:24.561 --> 00:17:26.466
<i>before he was captured
by the Nazis.</i>


00:17:26.496 --> 00:17:28.334
<i>Has she showed it to you?</i>


00:17:28.335 --> 00:17:30.805
Says she has it
memorized, sir.


00:17:30.835 --> 00:17:32.242
Blood hell!


00:17:32.272 --> 00:17:33.675
That changes things.


00:17:33.705 --> 00:17:35.078
One more thing, sir.


00:17:35.108 --> 00:17:36.577
We also appear
to have company.


00:17:36.607 --> 00:17:37.815
How many?


00:17:37.845 --> 00:17:39.316
Difficult to say.


00:17:39.346 --> 00:17:41.284
Looks like a transport
heading our way.


00:17:41.314 --> 00:17:43.884
Get your asses out of there
before they arrive!


00:17:43.885 --> 00:17:45.088
<i>Those are your orders!</i>


00:17:45.118 --> 00:17:47.554
Understood, sir.
F13C out.


00:17:50.223 --> 00:17:51.927
You don't trust me?


00:17:51.957 --> 00:17:53.661
They've arrived!


00:18:04.105 --> 00:18:08.076
It's the Germans.
On the left and right.


00:18:20.053 --> 00:18:22.589
We know you are in there!


00:18:22.619 --> 00:18:23.724
Come out!


00:19:23.416 --> 00:19:25.822
She's in there right now.


00:19:25.852 --> 00:19:30.657
Yes, sir, but she has been
joined by five BAF soldiers.


00:19:37.698 --> 00:19:39.266
And they are
in there right now?


00:19:39.296 --> 00:19:40.870
Are you sure?


00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:44.737
Yes, sir. They just arrived
maybe four or five minutes ago.


00:19:44.767 --> 00:19:46.340
They are well-armed.


00:19:55.983 --> 00:19:57.187
And the Americans?


00:19:57.217 --> 00:20:00.657
No, sir.
I have not seen them.


00:20:00.687 --> 00:20:03.323
And she has
the algorithm for sure?


00:20:04.858 --> 00:20:06.360
<i>Oui.</i>


00:20:08.329 --> 00:20:10.298
What is he doing?


00:20:33.119 --> 00:20:34.990
Excellent work.


00:20:35.020 --> 00:20:36.691
Merci, sir.


00:20:36.721 --> 00:20:38.392
May I leave?


00:20:42.797 --> 00:20:44.966
You have five seconds
to run for your life.


00:20:44.996 --> 00:20:48.505
No! No, sir!


00:20:48.535 --> 00:20:51.705
Sir, no!
Please! No, no!


00:21:07.821 --> 00:21:10.257
Damn it!


00:21:11.358 --> 00:21:12.663
The traitor sold us out.


00:21:12.693 --> 00:21:14.829
Let's concentrate
on the task in hand.


00:21:14.859 --> 00:21:16.363
I count ten men.


00:21:16.393 --> 00:21:18.081
Same here, sir.


00:21:18.111 --> 00:21:19.770
Can we trust you?


00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:22.606
I risked my life
to fight the Germans!


00:21:22.636 --> 00:21:25.606
I watched as my mother
and father begged for their life


00:21:25.636 --> 00:21:28.542
and the life
of my brother and sister!


00:21:28.572 --> 00:21:31.449
They were only eight
and nine years old!


00:21:31.479 --> 00:21:33.547
They'll do the same thing
to her if we leave her.


00:21:33.577 --> 00:21:35.482
No one said anything
about leaving her.


00:21:35.512 --> 00:21:37.221
We heard the colonel, sir.


00:21:37.251 --> 00:21:39.220
You swear you have
the algorithm?


00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:40.788
It's all I have!


00:21:44.591 --> 00:21:47.130
We know you are in there!


00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:50.697
To the British
soldiers inside:


00:21:50.727 --> 00:21:52.065
Send us the girl


00:21:52.066 --> 00:21:53.568
and you will all go free.


00:22:03.211 --> 00:22:06.381
Otherwise, you will
experience the same fate


00:22:06.411 --> 00:22:09.184
as your French friend here.


00:22:14.387 --> 00:22:17.759
She will never give
the algorithm to the Allies.


00:22:17.789 --> 00:22:19.230
Ever!


00:22:19.260 --> 00:22:21.896
You send her out,
you will all go free!


00:22:27.769 --> 00:22:31.839
You have two minutes
to send her out.


00:22:41.080 --> 00:22:42.052
No.


00:22:42.082 --> 00:22:43.320
No, no, please!


00:22:43.350 --> 00:22:45.819
Please! Please!
I am telling the truth!


00:22:45.849 --> 00:22:46.857
Please!


00:22:46.887 --> 00:22:50.157
Please, you must
believe me! Please!


00:22:50.187 --> 00:22:51.658
Gentlemen?


00:22:59.366 --> 00:23:01.169
Speak freely, lads.
You heard the colonel.


00:23:01.199 --> 00:23:02.936
You know the mission.


00:23:14.415 --> 00:23:16.087
Well, I want to go home.


00:23:16.117 --> 00:23:18.554
We don't even know
if she has the algorithm.


00:23:18.584 --> 00:23:21.021
And how do we know
this algorithm can even do


00:23:21.051 --> 00:23:22.656
what people say
it can?


00:23:25.525 --> 00:23:27.461
Give her to them.


00:23:27.462 --> 00:23:28.829
How can we really trust her?


00:23:34.935 --> 00:23:38.539
I couldn't live with myself
if we turned her in, sir.


00:23:38.569 --> 00:23:41.677
Let's complete the mission.


00:23:41.707 --> 00:23:43.577
I've always thought it's
a soldier's duty


00:23:43.578 --> 00:23:45.846
to protect those who
can't protect themselves.


00:23:45.876 --> 00:23:48.381
Now there are ten of them
to our five,


00:23:48.411 --> 00:23:50.887
but we have
the elevated position.


00:23:50.917 --> 00:23:53.454
But, Lieutenant, they may
have reinforcements?


00:23:53.484 --> 00:23:55.091
Yes, that's quite possible,
Harris.


00:23:55.121 --> 00:23:58.124
But sometimes a man has
to take a stand on principle.


00:23:58.125 --> 00:24:00.728
No matter the consequences.


00:24:02.462 --> 00:24:03.901
I'm with you, sir.


00:24:03.931 --> 00:24:06.668
You say and I'll fill them
so full of lead,


00:24:06.698 --> 00:24:08.569
it'll be coming
out their eyes.


00:24:19.347 --> 00:24:21.351
Thank you, gentlemen.


00:24:21.381 --> 00:24:23.884
You will not regret this!
Thank you.


00:24:27.487 --> 00:24:29.491
All right,
Fritz, we've talked.


00:24:29.521 --> 00:24:31.495
We're not
bringing her out,


00:24:31.525 --> 00:24:33.827
so you're gonna have
to come in and get her!


00:24:33.828 --> 00:24:35.629
Fire!


00:24:46.106 --> 00:24:48.041
Pull out!


00:24:49.243 --> 00:24:50.778
Pull out!


00:24:54.381 --> 00:24:55.600
Patch him up, man.


00:24:55.630 --> 00:24:56.819
Am I gonna die?


00:24:56.849 --> 00:24:59.437
- No.
- Am I gonna die?


00:24:59.467 --> 00:25:02.056
Am I gonna die?
Shit!


00:25:02.086 --> 00:25:03.725
Am I gonna die?


00:25:17.303 --> 00:25:19.072
Damn it!


00:25:25.846 --> 00:25:27.982
Sir!
I have some dynamite!


00:25:28.012 --> 00:25:29.020
Let me set a trap.


00:25:29.050 --> 00:25:31.519
I'll blow these bastards
to smithereens.


00:25:36.057 --> 00:25:38.126
Schreck!
I've got a schreck here!


00:25:38.156 --> 00:25:39.797
God, then
we're out-gunned!


00:25:39.827 --> 00:25:42.499
We gotta get outta here!
Any ideas?


00:25:42.529 --> 00:25:44.330
Let's go out the back way!
I know the forest!


00:25:44.360 --> 00:25:45.933
King, Walker, on Thomas!


00:25:45.963 --> 00:25:47.170
Go!


00:25:47.200 --> 00:25:48.636
Thomas, let's go!


00:26:53.134 --> 00:26:55.903
Let's keep moving.
Come on.


00:26:55.933 --> 00:26:57.070
Chins up.


00:27:00.840 --> 00:27:03.144
That's it.
This way.


00:27:08.515 --> 00:27:11.017
All right, mighty forty,
everyone down here.


00:27:40.214 --> 00:27:41.682
Come on!


00:27:43.916 --> 00:27:46.190
Stay with me. Come on.


00:27:46.220 --> 00:27:48.923
We're getting out of here.
We're getting out of here.


00:27:56.496 --> 00:27:58.031
Come on!
Hold it together, Thomas!


00:27:58.061 --> 00:27:59.403
We've got to move on, man!


00:27:59.433 --> 00:28:01.935
We're working
on this together.


00:28:01.965 --> 00:28:04.204
Pull it together, Thomas.


00:29:21.181 --> 00:29:23.869
So any chance of getting
medical support for Thomas?


00:29:23.899 --> 00:29:27.113
The wireless was destroyed.
There's no calling anyone.


00:29:27.143 --> 00:29:30.357
Are you sure we can trust
this location that he gave us?


00:29:30.387 --> 00:29:32.128
<i>Oui.</i>


00:29:32.158 --> 00:29:34.593
I mean, he was working for the
Germans, it may be compromised.


00:29:34.623 --> 00:29:36.098
I don't think so.


00:29:36.128 --> 00:29:38.965
I don't think Pierre expected
us to escape. You know?


00:29:38.995 --> 00:29:41.204
Yes. You may have a point.


00:29:41.234 --> 00:29:43.435
Damn it, we need a radio!
We need to pause!


00:29:43.465 --> 00:29:44.587
I know a safe house.


00:29:44.617 --> 00:29:45.739
It might have a radio.


00:29:45.740 --> 00:29:47.907
- How far?
- Not far.


00:31:06.686 --> 00:31:10.627
- Shit!
- Sir!


00:31:10.657 --> 00:31:12.827
Sir, he's not doing so well.


00:31:17.364 --> 00:31:19.700
Sir, they're getting closer.
We'll never outrun them.


00:31:19.730 --> 00:31:21.234
Especially with him
in this state.


00:31:21.264 --> 00:31:22.769
Well, we can't
just leave him here!


00:31:22.799 --> 00:31:23.904
You are...


00:31:25.406 --> 00:31:29.046
You have to.


00:31:29.076 --> 00:31:31.278
I'm not going to make it.


00:31:31.308 --> 00:31:32.782
I know that.


00:31:32.812 --> 00:31:34.180
And you know that.


00:31:34.181 --> 00:31:36.801
This can't
be all for nothing.


00:31:36.831 --> 00:31:39.451
You said we could
be heroes.


00:31:39.452 --> 00:31:41.454
Now get her to safety!


00:31:42.356 --> 00:31:44.126
You're coming with us, Thomas.


00:31:44.156 --> 00:31:46.260
We're gonna get you home
to see your wife and son.


00:31:46.290 --> 00:31:50.731
You lads can do it,
but not with me.


00:31:50.761 --> 00:31:53.436
Not with me!


00:31:53.466 --> 00:31:55.953
You get home to England.


00:31:55.983 --> 00:31:58.471
You tell my son what I did.


00:31:58.472 --> 00:32:02.242
You tell him I was a hero.


00:32:02.272 --> 00:32:03.512
I shall.


00:32:03.542 --> 00:32:05.312
Reach into my pocket.


00:32:05.342 --> 00:32:07.530
- Here.
- This one?


00:32:07.560 --> 00:32:09.748
There. There's a letter.


00:32:09.749 --> 00:32:13.957
Please...


00:32:13.987 --> 00:32:16.489
Please give this
to my wife.


00:32:16.490 --> 00:32:18.825
You tell her...


00:32:22.229 --> 00:32:24.631
You tell her that
I loved her the minute


00:32:24.661 --> 00:32:27.267
I have laid eyes
on her.


00:32:27.268 --> 00:32:29.472
I promise.


00:32:29.502 --> 00:32:31.706
You keep that promise.


00:32:31.736 --> 00:32:33.940
I will.
I will, Thomas.


00:32:33.941 --> 00:32:36.446
All right. Now...


00:32:36.476 --> 00:32:40.480
Now sit me up
against that tree.


00:32:46.820 --> 00:32:49.290
And hand me my gun.


00:32:53.126 --> 00:32:55.295
You don't have
to do this, Thomas.


00:32:55.325 --> 00:32:56.896
Yes, I do.


00:32:58.531 --> 00:32:59.532
Now go!


00:33:01.268 --> 00:33:06.273
Monsieur, I'm so sorry.


00:33:06.303 --> 00:33:08.007
Go!


00:33:25.759 --> 00:33:28.165
Let's go.


00:33:28.195 --> 00:33:31.197
Come on, you bloody krauts!


00:35:58.077 --> 00:35:59.178
<i>Schiesse!</i>


00:36:13.861 --> 00:36:16.949
That'll slow 'em down.
But it won't stop 'em.


00:36:16.979 --> 00:36:20.067
If Angelique's secret is
as valuable as we think,


00:36:20.097 --> 00:36:22.471
- then nothing will stop them.
- It is.


00:36:22.501 --> 00:36:25.271
Well, at least Thomas has bought us
enough time to gain some distance.


00:36:25.272 --> 00:36:28.241
It's just north,
a few kilometers.


00:36:28.271 --> 00:36:29.911
Let's move on.


00:36:29.941 --> 00:36:32.278
Everyone stays alert.


00:36:46.059 --> 00:36:47.530
We need to rest.


00:36:47.560 --> 00:36:51.231
All right, let's stop
just for a moment.


00:36:53.899 --> 00:36:55.769
Be sure and conserve water.


00:37:00.138 --> 00:37:02.776
These blisters are
killing me.


00:37:09.983 --> 00:37:12.218
Sir, I've got
ammunition here!


00:37:12.248 --> 00:37:13.787
Stop! Freeze, King!


00:37:17.990 --> 00:37:20.759
Don't move.


00:37:20.760 --> 00:37:23.162
Shit!


00:37:25.964 --> 00:37:28.968
Is it booby trapped?


00:37:28.998 --> 00:37:30.239
Yes, sir.


00:37:30.269 --> 00:37:32.538
With a compression mine.


00:37:32.539 --> 00:37:35.542
Attached to a grenade.
A stick grenade, sir.


00:37:37.577 --> 00:37:39.279
Do you see where
it's connected?


00:37:39.309 --> 00:37:41.983
Yes, sir.


00:37:42.013 --> 00:37:44.186
About six feet to my left.


00:37:44.216 --> 00:37:46.619
Mr. King, I need you
to ever so slightly


00:37:46.620 --> 00:37:48.125
point to where
the grenade is.


00:37:48.155 --> 00:37:50.323
Don't move your head
or your hips at all.


00:37:50.353 --> 00:37:51.328
Do you understand?


00:37:51.358 --> 00:37:54.127
Just turn your
wrist and point.


00:38:19.318 --> 00:38:21.487
Do you see it?


00:38:21.488 --> 00:38:22.791
Yes.


00:38:22.821 --> 00:38:24.390
Yes, I see it.


00:38:27.059 --> 00:38:28.928
Could we cut the wire?


00:38:37.070 --> 00:38:39.924
I need you to stay
very, very still.


00:38:39.954 --> 00:38:42.808
We're going to get you
out of this.


00:38:42.809 --> 00:38:46.879
You have to absolutely
not budge in the slightest.


00:38:46.909 --> 00:38:48.515
Yes, sir.


00:38:59.359 --> 00:39:02.065
How bad is it?


00:39:02.095 --> 00:39:03.800
They've double-rigged it.


00:39:03.830 --> 00:39:06.533
There's a compression mine
under the butt of the rifle.


00:39:08.633 --> 00:39:10.870
As long as he keeps pressure
on that, it won't detonate.


00:39:10.900 --> 00:39:13.539
But the wire that's
attached to the grenade


00:39:13.569 --> 00:39:15.212
is already
under tension.


00:39:15.242 --> 00:39:18.312
We clip that,
the charge will blow.


00:39:21.147 --> 00:39:22.818
Shit.


00:39:22.848 --> 00:39:24.251
What do we do?


00:40:19.606 --> 00:40:21.941
I'm never going to be with
a woman now, am I, sir?


00:40:21.971 --> 00:40:23.179
Stay calm, Mr. King.


00:40:23.209 --> 00:40:25.396
We've got to do something.


00:40:25.426 --> 00:40:27.583
He's already struggling.


00:40:27.613 --> 00:40:29.883
Those Nazis can't
be too far back.


00:40:34.620 --> 00:40:36.525
What are you thinking, sir?


00:40:36.555 --> 00:40:38.691
The only thing I can do
is try to tackle him


00:40:38.721 --> 00:40:40.225
out of the blast area.


00:40:40.255 --> 00:40:41.663
That's insane!


00:40:41.693 --> 00:40:43.496
And keep your
voice down, man!


00:40:43.497 --> 00:40:45.201
We need to keep him
steady.


00:40:45.231 --> 00:40:47.098
Are you losing your mind,
Lieutenant.


00:40:47.128 --> 00:40:48.672
With all due respect, sir.


00:40:48.702 --> 00:40:50.639
Well, do you have
a better idea?


00:40:50.669 --> 00:40:52.256
If we had something
to dampen the blast,


00:40:52.286 --> 00:40:53.873
then that would be
a fine thing, but...


00:40:53.874 --> 00:40:57.644
Any branches we might find
would just add to the shrapnel.


00:41:00.412 --> 00:41:02.284
I think I can get him clear.


00:41:02.314 --> 00:41:07.253
Sergeant Walker, if you
would accompany me over here,


00:41:07.254 --> 00:41:09.422
we can deduce
the blast radius.


00:41:09.452 --> 00:41:12.059
What are best chances are.


00:41:16.062 --> 00:41:18.964
Appears to be a slightly
angled towards 11:00.


00:41:21.234 --> 00:41:23.572
This direction.


00:41:23.602 --> 00:41:26.041
A radius nearly five feet.


00:41:26.071 --> 00:41:30.042
Should have two to three
seconds before it goes.


00:41:41.053 --> 00:41:42.891
Shall we?


00:41:42.921 --> 00:41:44.875
Seek out cover,
Sergeant Walker.


00:41:44.905 --> 00:41:46.829
What are you going
to do, sir?


00:41:46.859 --> 00:41:49.995
Here's what we're
going to do, Mr. King.


00:41:53.733 --> 00:41:56.239
I am going to tackle you.


00:41:56.269 --> 00:41:58.574
You are going to stay
absolutely still


00:41:58.604 --> 00:42:00.573
until you feel
my body slamming into yours.


00:42:00.603 --> 00:42:01.710
Do you understand that?


00:42:01.740 --> 00:42:05.177
Pardon, sir?
What did you say?


00:42:05.178 --> 00:42:06.781
Tackle you, King.


00:42:06.811 --> 00:42:08.415
It's our only option.


00:42:16.388 --> 00:42:17.626
I don't want to die, sir.


00:42:17.656 --> 00:42:20.262
But I don't want you
to die either, sir.


00:42:20.292 --> 00:42:23.829
Maybe not. Just move on and I'll take
care of this. Don't worry about it.


00:42:23.830 --> 00:42:26.199
None of us is going
to die, King.


00:42:26.229 --> 00:42:27.536
I can do this.


00:42:27.566 --> 00:42:30.202
But I need you to let me
do the work.


00:42:30.232 --> 00:42:31.503
Do you understand?


00:42:31.504 --> 00:42:33.873
If you move, you cost us
precious milliseconds.


00:42:33.903 --> 00:42:37.543
Let me move you.
You understand?


00:42:39.345 --> 00:42:40.747
Yes, sir.


00:42:43.515 --> 00:42:46.185
When are you going
to do this, sir?


00:42:52.492 --> 00:42:54.560
I shall give you
plenty of warning.


00:42:54.590 --> 00:42:56.128
Don't worry, Mr. King.


00:42:59.064 --> 00:43:00.599
Maybe it's not such
a good idea, sir.


00:43:00.600 --> 00:43:02.702
I mean, we could always
just cut the wire...


00:43:32.731 --> 00:43:33.966
You all right?


00:43:38.470 --> 00:43:39.905
Damn!


00:43:42.075 --> 00:43:44.179
Sorry, sir.
It's my fault. I'm sorry.


00:43:44.209 --> 00:43:48.380
All right, that's enough,
I'm alive. You're alive.


00:43:48.381 --> 00:43:50.149
This is not good.


00:43:52.718 --> 00:43:53.855
Shit.


00:43:53.885 --> 00:43:55.454
What's the diagnosis, man?


00:43:55.455 --> 00:43:58.892
Well, the good news is
you've got a clean open wound.


00:43:58.922 --> 00:44:01.594
Probably some
shrapnel tearing through.


00:44:01.624 --> 00:44:04.067
The bad news is this branch.


00:44:04.097 --> 00:44:06.868
Not much bleeding
because it's an impalement.


00:44:06.898 --> 00:44:09.669
But could have lacerated
your femoral artery.


00:44:09.699 --> 00:44:13.573
And you'd bleed
to death internally.


00:44:13.603 --> 00:44:15.641
And how do we know that?


00:44:15.671 --> 00:44:17.646
You'll know.


00:44:17.676 --> 00:44:20.146
I'll just plug this hole.


00:44:21.147 --> 00:44:22.250
Stop the bleeding.


00:44:22.280 --> 00:44:27.853
And then if I dress
this branch to stabilize it.


00:44:27.854 --> 00:44:30.207
Just do as little as
you need to, Harris.


00:44:30.237 --> 00:44:32.900
We don't have much time.
That's an order.


00:44:32.930 --> 00:44:35.593
It's good the house
is not far off, sir.


00:44:35.623 --> 00:44:37.731
Quick as you can, man.


00:44:41.600 --> 00:44:43.604
Can you walk?


00:44:43.634 --> 00:44:45.638
Yes. I can try.


00:44:45.668 --> 00:44:47.307
Come on.


00:46:50.296 --> 00:46:51.733
This is it.


00:46:51.763 --> 00:46:53.201
How are you doing, sir?


00:46:53.231 --> 00:46:55.500
Still planning on
surviving this bloody war.


00:46:55.501 --> 00:46:57.755
Are you sure this
place is safe?


00:46:57.785 --> 00:47:00.039
I'm not sure about
anything anymore,


00:47:00.069 --> 00:47:02.241
but what choice
do we have?


00:47:02.271 --> 00:47:04.709
Let's go.


00:47:22.829 --> 00:47:25.365
Come in. Quickly.
Quickly.


00:47:29.001 --> 00:47:30.335
Come on, sir.


00:47:33.338 --> 00:47:34.610
Come on.


00:47:34.640 --> 00:47:36.776
Easy, sir, easy.


00:47:45.885 --> 00:47:46.952
You quite all right,
Mr. Harris?


00:47:46.982 --> 00:47:48.123
Yes, sir, just need...


00:47:48.153 --> 00:47:50.192
Let me help.
I was a nurse.


00:47:50.222 --> 00:47:52.225
I worked at Clemenceau
Hospital before it was bombed.


00:47:52.255 --> 00:47:53.593
You...
you have a radio, yes?


00:47:53.623 --> 00:47:54.931
<i>Oui.</i>


00:47:54.961 --> 00:47:57.281
But it only hails frequencies
from the Resistance.


00:47:57.311 --> 00:47:59.631
Well, I mean, is there any
way that the Resistance


00:47:59.661 --> 00:48:01.600
can get in touch with
the allies so they can


00:48:01.630 --> 00:48:03.385
let them know our whereabouts?


00:48:03.415 --> 00:48:05.141
It is possible.
I can try.


00:48:05.171 --> 00:48:07.239
All right, Harris,
you accompany our friend


00:48:07.269 --> 00:48:08.675
and see if you
can achieve that.


00:48:15.948 --> 00:48:18.050
Because this did not
hit an artery,


00:48:18.051 --> 00:48:19.355
we can remove it.


00:48:19.385 --> 00:48:21.254
And you know this how,
from your time as a nurse?


00:48:21.284 --> 00:48:24.089
I shall get
some boiling water.


00:48:27.093 --> 00:48:28.697
Sir?


00:48:28.727 --> 00:48:30.766
Thank you.


00:48:30.796 --> 00:48:32.835
I was just doing my job.


00:48:32.865 --> 00:48:37.435
No, no, it's much more than just
doing your job saving my life.


00:48:37.465 --> 00:48:39.141
You're welcome, King.


00:48:39.171 --> 00:48:43.475
So, how's it going with
the French Resistance there?


00:48:43.505 --> 00:48:44.880
No.


00:48:44.910 --> 00:48:46.430
It's, it's
not like that.


00:48:46.460 --> 00:48:47.981
I'm sure
it's not, sir.


00:49:05.597 --> 00:49:07.466
This was a
good field dressing.


00:49:09.301 --> 00:49:11.571
I'll just leave her
to tend to your wounds, sir.


00:49:12.805 --> 00:49:14.009
What?


00:49:14.039 --> 00:49:17.547
Nothing.
He's just being an idiot.


00:49:17.577 --> 00:49:21.481
He's just a little boy who
needs the love of a woman.


00:49:21.511 --> 00:49:23.281
Yeah.


00:49:27.887 --> 00:49:29.821
F13C, come in, over.


00:49:32.624 --> 00:49:34.425
Is F13C checked in yet?


00:49:34.426 --> 00:49:36.012
Negative, sir.


00:49:36.042 --> 00:49:37.571
Raise them.


00:49:37.601 --> 00:49:39.131
Yes, sir.


00:49:43.736 --> 00:49:45.422
Okay, this is going to hurt.


00:49:45.452 --> 00:49:47.138
I wish I had
some whiskey or...


00:49:47.168 --> 00:49:48.556
I never touch the stuff.


00:49:48.586 --> 00:49:49.975
- No? Really?
- Really.


00:49:50.005 --> 00:49:52.311
Why not?


00:49:52.312 --> 00:49:53.315
It's okay. It's...


00:49:53.345 --> 00:49:54.847
it's none of my business.


00:49:56.347 --> 00:49:59.684
My father was rather
too fond of the stuff.


00:49:59.714 --> 00:50:01.453
Wasn't a great man.


00:50:05.091 --> 00:50:07.259
You're a great man.


00:50:07.289 --> 00:50:09.030
No.


00:50:09.060 --> 00:50:10.329
No, I'm just a soldier.


00:50:10.330 --> 00:50:13.066
No. You are so much
more than that.


00:50:21.506 --> 00:50:23.309
I'm sorry. I...


00:50:25.912 --> 00:50:27.946
God, that hurt.


00:50:27.976 --> 00:50:29.351
I'm sorry.


00:50:29.381 --> 00:50:31.050
I thought it was better
to take you by surprise.


00:50:31.080 --> 00:50:32.785
Well, you certainly did that.


00:50:32.815 --> 00:50:35.757
Dear God, that smarts.


00:50:35.787 --> 00:50:39.191
Okay, put pressure on there.


00:50:42.695 --> 00:50:44.196
Hold it.


00:50:54.906 --> 00:50:56.609
Thank you
for trusting me.


00:51:12.925 --> 00:51:14.926
I'll say this
for these Frenchmen:


00:51:14.956 --> 00:51:17.030
they make
a damn good wine.


00:51:18.765 --> 00:51:20.966
I'm a beer man,
myself.


00:51:20.996 --> 00:51:22.901
When in Rome.


00:51:22.931 --> 00:51:24.806
Drink up.


00:51:24.836 --> 00:51:27.472
You never know
when you...


00:51:32.412 --> 00:51:33.479
Right.


00:51:43.722 --> 00:51:46.492
Have you really never
been with a woman?


00:51:50.196 --> 00:51:53.766
Well, I mean
I've kissed 'em.


00:51:53.796 --> 00:51:54.737
Lots of them.


00:51:54.767 --> 00:51:58.088
But, no,
not all the way.


00:51:58.118 --> 00:52:01.439
You're missing out, mate.


00:52:01.469 --> 00:52:03.078
Well...


00:52:03.108 --> 00:52:05.611
To me,
it's not just about sex.


00:52:08.379 --> 00:52:13.051
The more you have of a thing,
the less special it becomes.


00:52:13.081 --> 00:52:16.190
At least to me.


00:52:16.220 --> 00:52:18.156
I've always wanted it
to be with the right woman.


00:52:18.186 --> 00:52:21.394
Mate, they're all
the right woman.


00:52:26.966 --> 00:52:28.471
Hey, to be honest
with you,


00:52:28.501 --> 00:52:31.537
my first time I was
head over heels in love.


00:52:34.906 --> 00:52:38.778
We were just kids with
no idea what we were doing.


00:52:42.714 --> 00:52:44.216
But it was real.


00:52:54.526 --> 00:52:56.596
I can't imagine what I'm going
to tell Mrs. Thomas.


00:53:00.298 --> 00:53:03.034
You are going to tell her
that her man was a hero,


00:53:03.035 --> 00:53:06.406
and we wouldn't be here
if he hadn't done what he did.


00:53:08.073 --> 00:53:10.409
And if you want,
I'll go with you.


00:53:12.477 --> 00:53:14.780
Thank you.


00:53:20.285 --> 00:53:22.187
You're a good man,
Mr. Walker.


00:53:23.988 --> 00:53:27.592
No. I'm not.


00:53:29.928 --> 00:53:31.696
But I'm trying.


00:53:35.667 --> 00:53:37.670
You have your moments.


00:53:37.700 --> 00:53:39.704
All it takes is one.


00:53:40.838 --> 00:53:42.808
One good one.


00:53:47.245 --> 00:53:49.714
You should wait
for the right woman, King.


00:54:42.734 --> 00:54:46.037
F13C, this is 7, 8,
Echo, Charlie, Papa.


00:54:46.067 --> 00:54:47.710
Come in, over.


00:54:47.740 --> 00:54:53.946
Again, F13C,
this is 78ECP.


00:54:53.976 --> 00:54:55.247
Come in, over.


00:54:56.649 --> 00:54:58.484
There... there's
no response, sir.


00:54:58.514 --> 00:55:00.819
- Keep scanning.
- Yes, sir.


00:55:10.629 --> 00:55:12.735
F13C here.


00:55:12.765 --> 00:55:14.170
Are you there, Dunkirk?


00:55:14.200 --> 00:55:17.836
Repeat, F13C,
are you there, Dunkirk?


00:55:17.866 --> 00:55:19.907
F13C here.


00:55:19.937 --> 00:55:22.273
Are you there, Dunkirk?


00:55:22.274 --> 00:55:25.012
Repeat, F13C here.


00:55:25.042 --> 00:55:27.046
Are you there, Dunkirk?


00:55:27.076 --> 00:55:28.847
F13C, come in.


00:55:34.320 --> 00:55:35.590
Keep searching.


00:55:35.620 --> 00:55:37.656
He may be using
a different frequency.


00:55:40.892 --> 00:55:42.963
<i>F13C here.</i>


00:55:42.993 --> 00:55:44.829
<i>Are you there, Dunkirk?</i>


00:55:44.830 --> 00:55:46.201
We have a signal, sir.


00:55:46.231 --> 00:55:48.835
<i>F13C here.
Are you there, Dunkirk?</i>


00:55:48.865 --> 00:55:51.469
F13C.
This is Colonel Plummer.


00:55:51.470 --> 00:55:53.842
<i>What is your sitrep?</i>


00:55:53.872 --> 00:55:56.045
Repeat, what is your sitrep?


00:55:56.075 --> 00:56:00.212
We're at a safe house,
outside the drop coordinates,


00:56:00.242 --> 00:56:03.131
approximately
four miles northwest.


00:56:03.161 --> 00:56:06.051
Good to hear
your voices, boys.


00:56:06.081 --> 00:56:07.188
What's your situation?


00:56:07.218 --> 00:56:09.554
<i>We've lost Sgt. Thomas.</i>


00:56:09.555 --> 00:56:11.525
<i>Lieutenant Calloway
is injured,</i>


00:56:11.555 --> 00:56:13.496
but we have
secured the package.


00:56:13.526 --> 00:56:15.665
<i>We're being pursued
by Jerrys, sir.</i>


00:56:15.695 --> 00:56:18.132
<i>We're possibly going
to need air support.</i>


00:56:18.162 --> 00:56:21.733
French Resistance have had
a change of plans, so we...


00:56:21.763 --> 00:56:23.669
we may have
been compromised.


00:56:24.903 --> 00:56:26.775
Where are you heading?


00:56:26.805 --> 00:56:31.344
<i>We're heading to an airfield
about two miles from the bridge.</i>


00:56:31.374 --> 00:56:33.681
<i>The package will be
flown to mainland.</i>


00:56:33.711 --> 00:56:35.516
<i>Sir, we're going
to have to pass through</i>


00:56:35.546 --> 00:56:38.282
<i>German-occupied area
to get to the airfield.</i>


00:56:38.283 --> 00:56:39.721
<i>We may need support.</i>


00:56:39.751 --> 00:56:43.607
I'll do my best
to provide some air support.


00:56:43.637 --> 00:56:47.493
Pop some smoke so
we know where you are.


00:56:47.523 --> 00:56:48.496
<i>One more thing.</i>


00:56:48.526 --> 00:56:50.065
What's that, Colonel?


00:56:50.095 --> 00:56:53.703
There should be a bridge a few
kilometers down the main route.


00:56:53.733 --> 00:56:57.970
<i>We have reason to believe there's a
German patrol operating in that area.</i>


00:56:58.000 --> 00:57:02.041
<i>That would put a group of French
freedom fighters in danger.</i>


00:57:02.071 --> 00:57:06.410
I want you boys
to blow that bridge.


00:57:06.440 --> 00:57:07.882
But with what, sir?


00:57:07.912 --> 00:57:11.516
Walker should have
the explosives you boys need.


00:57:11.517 --> 00:57:14.287
Roger that. Out.


00:57:19.591 --> 00:57:22.560
Tell headquarters we should
send men to the bridge


00:57:22.590 --> 00:57:25.097
and to the airstrip.


00:57:37.108 --> 00:57:38.877
We have more company.


00:57:53.291 --> 00:57:54.693
Quietly.


00:58:02.033 --> 00:58:03.237
That's gotta sting.


00:58:03.267 --> 00:58:04.620
Mr. Keller, do you drink?


00:58:04.650 --> 00:58:06.004
As much as I can, ma'am.


00:58:12.044 --> 00:58:14.946
This looks like
it's going to be fine.


00:58:14.976 --> 00:58:16.083
I'll live.


00:58:16.113 --> 00:58:17.416
We'll all will.


00:58:38.303 --> 00:58:40.857
Do you see any more?


00:58:40.887 --> 00:58:43.441
Let's hide the bodies.


00:58:48.314 --> 00:58:50.049
<i>Nein.</i>


00:59:04.028 --> 00:59:06.097
<i>Ja wohl.</i>


00:59:16.106 --> 00:59:17.275
You talked to the Colonel?


00:59:17.276 --> 00:59:19.614
- Yes.
- What does he say?


00:59:19.644 --> 00:59:21.280
I managed to give him
our coordinates and then...


00:59:21.310 --> 00:59:22.451
We're out of time, sir.


00:59:22.481 --> 00:59:24.186
Why?
What's... what's happening?


00:59:24.216 --> 00:59:26.785
We just killed two Nazis who were
about to call in our position.


00:59:26.815 --> 00:59:28.757
- Damn it.
- Can you walk?


00:59:28.787 --> 00:59:30.388
Doesn't look like
I have much choice, does it?


00:59:30.418 --> 00:59:32.607
Come on, sir.
Come on.


00:59:32.637 --> 00:59:34.826
That's it.
All right.


00:59:34.827 --> 00:59:36.729
<i>Merci.</i>


00:59:51.042 --> 00:59:54.211
The airfield is
15 kilometers north.


00:59:54.241 --> 00:59:55.250
<i>Merci.</i>


00:59:55.280 --> 00:59:56.518
<i>Merci beaucoup.</i>


00:59:56.548 --> 00:59:58.654
So, yeah, thank you
for what you are doing.


00:59:58.684 --> 01:00:01.252
The Nazis are coming. You cannot
stay here, you know that.


01:00:01.282 --> 01:00:02.556
I know.


01:00:02.586 --> 01:00:04.956
I'm going to try
and buy you some more time.


01:00:06.124 --> 01:00:07.593
<i>Merci.</i>


01:00:08.993 --> 01:00:10.829
Sir, are you sure you don't
want any of that morphine?


01:00:10.859 --> 01:00:13.064
No, thank you, Harris.
It dulls the senses.


01:00:13.094 --> 01:00:15.300
Yeah, but so does having
a tree in your leg.


01:01:09.187 --> 01:01:10.891
<i>Bonjour.</i>


01:01:10.921 --> 01:01:12.625
No, no, no.


01:01:21.934 --> 01:01:25.137
It's a rather nice day
for a stroll, isn't it?


01:01:28.205 --> 01:01:31.709
And where is our French
little mouse strolling to?


01:01:37.548 --> 01:01:40.818
We can make this so much simpler
if you just tell me where she is.


01:01:42.620 --> 01:01:43.590
Who?


01:01:43.620 --> 01:01:45.791
What girl?


01:01:48.258 --> 01:01:50.162
Bring him.


01:01:50.192 --> 01:01:52.197
No, no.


01:01:52.227 --> 01:01:54.233
Wait. Wait.


01:01:57.669 --> 01:02:00.705
I don't under...
What is going...


01:03:13.512 --> 01:03:16.749
I love the smell
of burning flesh.


01:03:19.684 --> 01:03:24.326
It reminds me of how,
as a little boy,


01:03:24.356 --> 01:03:29.093
<i>my father would roast
a schwein on an open fire.</i>


01:03:37.769 --> 01:03:40.272
Now, tell me where they are.


01:03:44.575 --> 01:03:47.945
I don't know what
you're talking about.


01:04:10.328 --> 01:04:13.197
Now tell me everything
or you will die.


01:04:14.132 --> 01:04:17.535
Okay, okay.


01:04:20.838 --> 01:04:22.974
Everything, I'll tell you.


01:04:26.043 --> 01:04:29.084
They are...


01:04:29.114 --> 01:04:31.250
heading into the village.


01:04:37.188 --> 01:04:42.027
Now, why would they
be going into a village


01:04:42.057 --> 01:04:45.230
that is crawling
with Germans?


01:04:47.931 --> 01:04:50.971
Ex... exactly.


01:04:51.001 --> 01:04:54.405
That is the last place you
would expect to see them.


01:04:57.175 --> 01:05:01.780
Do I look,
stupid to you?


01:05:01.810 --> 01:05:03.648
Honest answer?


01:05:07.918 --> 01:05:09.187
<i>Oui.</i>


01:05:13.491 --> 01:05:15.427
So be it.


01:05:19.797 --> 01:05:23.901
For your information,
I know that the girl


01:05:23.902 --> 01:05:29.441
is trying to escape by plane
from a small airfield.


01:05:32.943 --> 01:05:35.146
Not so stupid now, am I?


01:06:26.533 --> 01:06:28.336
Do you need to stop?


01:06:30.870 --> 01:06:32.506
Perhaps just
for a moment.


01:06:40.113 --> 01:06:43.353
By my calculations,
we are here,


01:06:43.383 --> 01:06:46.186
so it should be just
beyond this next ridge.


01:06:46.216 --> 01:06:47.921
You're never gonna
make it on that leg.


01:06:47.951 --> 01:06:49.522
That's at least
another six miles.


01:06:49.552 --> 01:06:50.627
I'll manage.


01:06:50.657 --> 01:06:52.894
You may not have to.


01:06:55.528 --> 01:06:57.097
What do you mean?


01:06:59.300 --> 01:07:00.802
Well, shit.


01:07:00.832 --> 01:07:02.335
Take cover.


01:07:22.122 --> 01:07:24.023
You know, I could probably
just pick him off


01:07:24.024 --> 01:07:26.426
from about a hundred
yards with this rifle.


01:07:26.456 --> 01:07:28.628
You snipers are
all the same.


01:07:28.629 --> 01:07:32.633
Trust me, mate, these blokes
will piss their pants.


01:07:32.663 --> 01:07:34.702
Yes, well, we'll see
about that, won't we?


01:07:57.289 --> 01:07:59.159
Be ready,
here they come.


01:08:15.108 --> 01:08:18.980
Help! Help!


01:08:20.213 --> 01:08:22.314
Don't shoot.
Don't shoot.


01:08:22.315 --> 01:08:24.018
Please, no, don't shoot.


01:08:24.048 --> 01:08:25.751
Don't shoot.
Don't shoot.


01:08:25.752 --> 01:08:27.488
Don't shoot me.
Please, no, don't shoot.


01:08:27.518 --> 01:08:29.522
Don't shoot.
Don't shoot, please.


01:08:29.552 --> 01:08:31.492
Hello, mates.


01:08:38.164 --> 01:08:40.368
Good afternoon, gentlemen.


01:08:44.538 --> 01:08:46.075
I can't believe
that worked.


01:08:46.105 --> 01:08:47.940
What would you do
if a big bald bastard


01:08:47.970 --> 01:08:50.043
tossed a grenade
in your vehicle?


01:08:50.073 --> 01:08:51.511
Fair point.


01:09:25.078 --> 01:09:26.597
It's quiet.
I don't like it.


01:09:26.627 --> 01:09:28.117
This should do the trick.


01:09:28.147 --> 01:09:29.516
Once we destroy it,
that should slow them down.


01:09:29.546 --> 01:09:30.783
- Mr. Harris?
- Sir?


01:09:30.813 --> 01:09:32.051
You stay and look out.


01:09:32.052 --> 01:09:34.187
Mr. King, Mr. Walker, would
you kindly assist me in rigging?


01:09:34.217 --> 01:09:35.955
The pleasure would
be mine, sir.


01:09:35.985 --> 01:09:37.361
Come along, King.


01:09:37.391 --> 01:09:39.827
You seem to like
explosives today.


01:10:49.195 --> 01:10:50.829
How are we doing, gentlemen?


01:10:50.859 --> 01:10:52.882
Getting there, sir.


01:10:52.912 --> 01:10:54.905
Sergeant Walker?


01:10:54.935 --> 01:10:56.602
A few more moments, please.


01:10:56.632 --> 01:10:57.704
Very well.


01:11:01.541 --> 01:11:03.709
How's it going
down there, chaps?


01:11:03.739 --> 01:11:05.028
Almost done.


01:11:05.058 --> 01:11:06.347
Make it quick.


01:11:09.583 --> 01:11:13.057
Is this the bridge?
Here?


01:11:13.087 --> 01:11:14.958
The open space on the other
side of this tree line


01:11:14.988 --> 01:11:18.191
has a hangar-like structure.
It's got to be the way out.


01:11:19.626 --> 01:11:21.429
Sir, if I'm reading
this map correctly,


01:11:21.459 --> 01:11:23.262
then the airfield
should just be on


01:11:23.292 --> 01:11:24.735
the other side of this forest.


01:11:24.765 --> 01:11:26.699
- Where's Walker and King?
- Just finishing up.


01:11:26.729 --> 01:11:28.135
They should be up
momentarily.


01:11:28.165 --> 01:11:29.436
I hope so.


01:11:33.006 --> 01:11:33.977
Do you hear that?


01:11:34.007 --> 01:11:35.379
That doesn't sound good.


01:11:35.409 --> 01:11:37.311
Doesn't sound like
a lot of fun.


01:11:37.341 --> 01:11:38.912
Mr. Walker?


01:11:38.913 --> 01:11:40.147
How are we
doing down there?


01:11:40.177 --> 01:11:41.584
Almost there, sir.


01:11:41.614 --> 01:11:44.385
Well, hurry up!
We have to go!


01:11:53.327 --> 01:11:55.529
- Start the car.
- It won't start, sir.


01:11:55.559 --> 01:11:56.932
Quick as you can, man.


01:11:56.962 --> 01:11:58.631
It won't start, sir.
It won't start.


01:11:58.632 --> 01:12:00.768
- Let's go!
- It won't start.


01:12:21.521 --> 01:12:24.890
Drop your weapons
and surrender.


01:12:24.891 --> 01:12:27.498
You have nowhere to go.


01:12:27.528 --> 01:12:31.049
It's a bloody tank.
Damn it.


01:12:31.079 --> 01:12:34.601
This is your final warning.


01:12:36.569 --> 01:12:39.271
Drop your weapons
and surrender.


01:12:39.301 --> 01:12:41.941
Damn, it's a ruddy tank!


01:12:44.177 --> 01:12:46.145
- We'll have to go on foot!
- Let's go!


01:12:48.181 --> 01:12:49.483
Go, go, go!


01:12:51.217 --> 01:12:54.120
Fire!


01:13:54.780 --> 01:13:57.984
Did you really think that
you could escape from me?


01:13:58.014 --> 01:14:00.821
We monitored
your radio transmissions.


01:15:17.965 --> 01:15:19.401
Are we good?


01:15:19.431 --> 01:15:20.868
We're good.


01:15:33.012 --> 01:15:35.614
I do not understand
how anyone could like


01:15:35.644 --> 01:15:37.784
such an inferior race.


01:15:39.520 --> 01:15:42.190
They're all like rats.


01:15:42.220 --> 01:15:44.861
Don't you know this?


01:15:44.891 --> 01:15:48.261
All they have
ever done was lie,


01:15:48.291 --> 01:15:51.031
steal, and cheat.


01:15:52.565 --> 01:15:54.635
And you support them?


01:15:56.435 --> 01:16:01.807
Now, we could have easily
slaughtered you Brits at Dunkirk.


01:16:01.837 --> 01:16:04.843
But we offered you
a second chance,


01:16:04.873 --> 01:16:07.817
a chance to align with us.


01:16:07.847 --> 01:16:12.151
Let's just see if your
Mr. Winston Churchill


01:16:12.181 --> 01:16:14.223
makes the right decision.


01:16:14.253 --> 01:16:17.441
If it were up to me,
I would have killed


01:16:17.471 --> 01:16:20.660
every last one
of you on that beach.


01:16:21.961 --> 01:16:24.998
But you will all
die here today.


01:16:26.365 --> 01:16:28.135
Do you realize this?


01:16:32.437 --> 01:16:34.173
And I will decide how.


01:16:38.677 --> 01:16:42.414
And as for you, French,


01:16:42.444 --> 01:16:44.984
you disgust me!


01:16:57.597 --> 01:17:00.851
Now personally, I would love


01:17:00.881 --> 01:17:04.136
to kill you
right here and now.


01:17:08.408 --> 01:17:11.313
But apparently...


01:17:11.343 --> 01:17:17.216
You have some information in that
French little brain of yours.


01:17:22.721 --> 01:17:27.293
That is very valuable
to us.


01:17:35.101 --> 01:17:38.972
Now, I will ask you
one simple question


01:17:40.873 --> 01:17:43.609
and you will answer me.


01:17:45.377 --> 01:17:47.647
What is the algorithm?


01:18:07.734 --> 01:18:12.873
What is the algorithm!?


01:18:14.440 --> 01:18:16.042
Bitch.


01:18:20.547 --> 01:18:22.384
I will count down from five,


01:18:22.414 --> 01:18:24.283
and then you will tell me
the algorithm.


01:18:26.720 --> 01:18:28.387
Okay. I will tell you!
I will tell you.


01:18:28.417 --> 01:18:29.655
Don't tell him anything!


01:18:33.927 --> 01:18:34.962
<i>Zwei.</i>


01:18:36.930 --> 01:18:37.897
<i>Eins.</i>


01:19:49.235 --> 01:19:51.337
You go on ahead.
I'll catch you up.


01:19:51.367 --> 01:19:52.538
Let me help you, sir.


01:19:59.445 --> 01:20:00.980
Fire!


01:20:03.583 --> 01:20:05.352
Cover and fire!


01:20:22.903 --> 01:20:24.870
Take cover!


01:20:48.761 --> 01:20:50.199
You all right, Mr. King?


01:20:50.229 --> 01:20:52.298
Yes, sir, just a nick.
I'm fine.


01:20:54.699 --> 01:20:56.736
All right.
Stay low. Stay low.


01:20:58.870 --> 01:21:00.873
We need to slow them down.


01:21:24.931 --> 01:21:26.832
You have nowhere to go!


01:21:26.862 --> 01:21:28.769
Surrender!


01:21:30.369 --> 01:21:32.805
More tension.
More tension.


01:21:34.539 --> 01:21:39.311
Surrender and give us the girl
and you will all go free.


01:21:43.882 --> 01:21:46.103
You will not escape.


01:21:46.133 --> 01:21:48.324
You will not get away.


01:21:48.354 --> 01:21:51.057
No one's going
to surrender, Fritz.


01:21:58.064 --> 01:21:59.499
How we doing, lads?


01:21:59.529 --> 01:22:01.534
One minute.


01:22:13.846 --> 01:22:15.985
Surrender!


01:22:16.015 --> 01:22:18.118
Okay, we're so close.


01:22:19.319 --> 01:22:20.255
Ready, sir.


01:22:20.285 --> 01:22:22.057
You will not
get out of there.


01:22:22.087 --> 01:22:24.423
Lay down covering fire
and move on my three,


01:22:24.453 --> 01:22:26.825
two, one... fire!


01:22:32.966 --> 01:22:34.151
Shit.


01:22:34.181 --> 01:22:35.367
Move!


01:22:36.970 --> 01:22:38.571
Move! Move!


01:22:39.672 --> 01:22:41.474
Go, go, go.


01:24:17.602 --> 01:24:19.541
For King and country.


01:24:19.571 --> 01:24:21.541
I'm willing to bet
Fritz is still coming.


01:24:21.571 --> 01:24:23.142
So let's go.


01:24:30.917 --> 01:24:32.254
Where is the plane?


01:24:32.284 --> 01:24:33.586
It's supposed to be here.


01:24:42.528 --> 01:24:44.129
No!


01:25:03.682 --> 01:25:05.284
You have nowhere to go!


01:25:11.157 --> 01:25:13.196
Surrender.


01:25:13.226 --> 01:25:16.996
Brother by my side,
what do you want to do?


01:25:17.026 --> 01:25:18.897
I have one magazine left.


01:25:18.927 --> 01:25:20.602
No. No.


01:25:20.632 --> 01:25:22.767
Drop your weapons.


01:25:22.797 --> 01:25:24.503
Do it now!


01:25:29.342 --> 01:25:32.045
You are totally surrounded.


01:25:34.779 --> 01:25:36.515
Bloody hell, I'm not
going out like this.


01:25:36.516 --> 01:25:38.718
- No!
- Stand down, Sergeant Walker.


01:25:38.748 --> 01:25:40.519
It's our only chance.


01:25:44.989 --> 01:25:46.960
I'm sorry, Angelique.


01:25:46.990 --> 01:25:48.660
We did all we could.


01:25:48.690 --> 01:25:50.145
Please, no.
Please, no.


01:25:50.175 --> 01:25:51.601
Please don't give up hope.


01:25:51.631 --> 01:25:54.367
It wasn't supposed
to end like this.


01:25:56.401 --> 01:25:57.703
Fire.


01:25:59.004 --> 01:26:01.106
Look. Look!


01:26:07.113 --> 01:26:08.785
It's our boys.


01:26:08.815 --> 01:26:10.717
It's about bloody time.


01:26:55.962 --> 01:26:57.530
<i>Schiesse.</i>


01:26:59.030 --> 01:27:00.833
<i>Schiesse.</i>


01:27:55.120 --> 01:27:58.856
See, you never
give up hope.


01:27:58.886 --> 01:28:00.396
We did it.


01:28:00.426 --> 01:28:03.631
God save the King.


01:28:03.661 --> 01:28:06.866
We did it.
We did it!


01:28:15.574 --> 01:28:16.879
Let's get her to that plane.


01:28:16.909 --> 01:28:19.679
You took the words
right out of my mouth.


01:29:05.056 --> 01:29:06.693
Thank you.


01:29:08.159 --> 01:29:09.695
Thank you.


01:29:11.596 --> 01:29:13.131
I'm sorry for your men.


01:29:13.132 --> 01:29:15.538
But thank you for my life.


01:29:15.568 --> 01:29:18.271
I just hope it
was worth it, love.


01:29:18.301 --> 01:29:20.439
It is.


01:29:25.444 --> 01:29:27.115
Could you do us a favor?


01:29:27.145 --> 01:29:30.581
When you get back to London,
find Emily Thomas.


01:29:30.582 --> 01:29:32.687
Give her this letter.


01:29:32.717 --> 01:29:34.820
I don't think I'll be around
to give it to her.


01:29:34.850 --> 01:29:36.954
And I'd rather she got it
sooner than later.


01:29:36.984 --> 01:29:38.456
Of course.


01:29:38.486 --> 01:29:39.958
Thank you.


01:29:44.663 --> 01:29:47.499
Let's get you on that plane.


01:29:47.529 --> 01:29:49.502
Are you all right?


01:29:49.532 --> 01:29:51.240
You?


01:29:51.270 --> 01:29:53.342
I'm alive.


01:29:53.372 --> 01:29:55.559
I don't know how,
but I am.


01:29:55.589 --> 01:29:57.746
You must never
give up hope.


01:29:57.776 --> 01:30:00.863
It doesn't matter how,
it matters why.


01:30:00.893 --> 01:30:03.981
You are a special man,
Lieutenant.


01:30:04.011 --> 01:30:05.916
You have a purpose.


01:30:05.946 --> 01:30:07.852
You must trust that.


01:30:07.882 --> 01:30:09.592
Thank you.


01:30:09.622 --> 01:30:12.527
Those men died heroes.


01:30:12.557 --> 01:30:14.694
Is there a better way
to serve your country?


01:30:14.724 --> 01:30:16.264
None.


01:30:16.294 --> 01:30:18.115
What will you do now?


01:30:18.145 --> 01:30:19.966
Will I see you again?


01:30:22.235 --> 01:30:24.272
This war is
far from over.


01:30:24.302 --> 01:30:29.240
I'll just have to enjoy the
beauty this world has to offer.


01:30:29.270 --> 01:30:32.912
When one remembers to
look beyond the ugliness.


01:30:49.294 --> 01:30:51.032
I'll see you in London.


01:30:51.062 --> 01:30:53.833
Now, let's get you
on that plane.


01:31:43.815 --> 01:31:45.583
I think she
likes you, sir.


01:31:45.613 --> 01:31:47.885
I don't know.


01:31:47.886 --> 01:31:50.323
Did you see the way
she looked at me just now?


01:31:50.353 --> 01:31:52.291
There might be
a real future there.


01:31:55.321 --> 01:32:13.321
<font color=#ff0000>subs4free.info</font>

